---
import MainLayout from "../../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";

// We use the high-end hero image generated
import blogHero from "../../../assets/soberania-digital.png";
---

<MainLayout title="Digital Sovereignty: Why you should stop building on rented ground | Otterock Blog">
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-20 px-6">
    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <a
        href="/en/blog"
        class="inline-block mb-8 text-sm text-otter-deep font-bold hover:text-otter-accent transition-colors hover:underline underline-offset-4"
      >
        ← Back to Blog
      </a>

      <span
        class="text-slate-600 font-bold tracking-widest uppercase text-xs mb-4 block font-body"
      >
        Strategy • 5 min read
      </span>

      <h1
        class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-black text-otter-deep mb-6 leading-tight font-display"
      >
        Digital Sovereignty: Why you should stop building your business on rented ground
      </h1>

      <p class="text-xl text-slate-700 italic font-body mb-8">
        "If your only digital presence depends on an external platform, you don't have a solid business; you have a room decorated in a hotel that doesn't belong to you."
      </p>

      <div
        class="rounded-3xl overflow-hidden shadow-xl mb-12 aspect-video bg-otter-deep"
      >
        <Image
          src={blogHero}
          alt="Digital Sovereignty and Digital Craftsmanship"
          width={800}
          quality="mid"
          format="webp"
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          class="w-full h-full object-cover opacity-90"
        />
      </div>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-lg text-slate-700 leading-relaxed font-body">
      <p
        class="first-letter:text-5xl first-letter:font-bold first-letter:text-otter-deep first-letter:mr-2 first-letter:float-left"
      >
        Imagine you wake up tomorrow and your favorite social network has decided to close your account, or worse, has changed its algorithm and now nobody sees what you post. For many entrepreneurs, this is not a nightmare, it is a real vulnerability.
      </p>

      <p>
        In this post, we talk about <strong>Digital Sovereignty</strong> and why it is your brand's most valuable asset.
      </p>

      <hr class="border-otter-deep/10 my-12" />

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-6 font-display">
          1. The risk of "Rented Ground"
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Platforms like Instagram, TikTok, or Booking are incredible visibility tools, but they have a problem: you don't set the rules.
        </p>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4 text-slate-700 mb-8">
          <li>
            <strong>The Algorithm is the owner:</strong> It decides who sees you and when.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>The Data isn't yours:</strong> You don't have real access to your followers' database.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Identity is limited:</strong> You will always be under the design and limitations of another.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Building your business exclusively there is like building a mansion on rented land. If the owner of the plot decides to raise the rent or close the place, you lose your investment.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-6 font-display mt-12">
          2. Your Web: Your Land, Your Rock
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Digital Craftsmanship was born to give you back control. Having your own website, developed with high-level technology, means that you are the owner of the plot.
        </p>

        <div
          class="bg-otter-sand/50 p-6 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-otter-deep my-8"
        >
          <ul class="space-y-4">
            <li>
              <strong class="text-otter-deep font-bold">Total Experience Control:</strong>
              <p class="text-sm mt-1 text-slate-800">
                On your website, clean of distractions from notifications or advertising from the competition, you guide your customer's path from interest to booking or purchase.
              </p>
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong class="text-otter-deep font-bold">Technological Independence:</strong>
              <p class="text-sm mt-1 text-slate-800">
                By using tools like Astro, we guarantee that your site is fast and efficient, without depending on heavy "builders" that keep you tied to their monthly fees.
              </p>
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-6 font-display mt-12">
          3. Data is the new Gold
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          Digital sovereignty is not just about aesthetics; it is about business intelligence.
          When you have your own platform (backed by solid databases like Supabase), every interaction counts:
        </p>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-slate-700 italic mb-8">
          <li>You know what your customers are looking for.</li>
          <li>You have their emails and contacts safely and directly.</li>
          <li>You can automate processes with n8n so your business works while you rest.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-center font-bold text-otter-deep text-xl mt-8">
          This isn't just a page; it's an infrastructure of freedom.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-6 font-display mt-12">
          4. The Value of Hand-Made
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-6">
          At Otterock, we understand that your project has soul. That's why we don't deliver mass-produced solutions. Digital sovereignty requires a firm foundation like a rock and a fluid execution like an otter.
        </p>
        
        <p>
          Our mission is for you to stop being an internet tenant and become the owner of your digital ecosystem. Because when the code is artisanal, independence is total.
        </p>
      </section>

      <hr class="border-otter-deep/10 my-12" />

      <section class="text-center">
        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-otter-deep mb-6 font-display">
          Conclusion
        </h2>
        <p class="mb-8">
          The digital world changes fast, but the assets you own are the only ones that will give you long-term peace of mind. Don't leave the future of your brand in the hands of an algorithm. It's time to claim your sovereignty.
        </p>
        <p class="text-2xl font-black text-otter-deep mb-12">
          Is your business truly yours or does it belong to a social network?
        </p>
      </section>

      <section
        class="bg-otter-deep text-white p-8 md:p-12 rounded-3xl text-center relative overflow-hidden"
      >
        <div
          class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-32 h-32 bg-white/10 rounded-full -mr-10 -mt-10 blur-2xl"
        >
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold font-display mb-4 relative z-10">
          Ready to own your plot?
        </h3>
        <p class="mb-8 opacity-90 leading-relaxed relative z-10">
          Let's build together a platform that belongs to you 100%. No strings attached, no limits, with an artisan soul.
        </p>

        <a
          href="/en/contacto"
          class="inline-block bg-white text-otter-deep px-8 py-4 rounded-full font-bold hover:bg-otter-accent hover:text-white transition-all hover:-translate-y-1 shadow-lg relative z-10"
        >
          Let's talk about your digital sovereignty
        </a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</MainLayout>
